WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.240
What lies west of the Sunset Sea? What secrets&nbsp;
does the empire of Yi Ti hold in the east?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.880
Could we hear more about John Snow in the north?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.167
There's no chance these "Game of&nbsp;
Thrones" spin-offs could go south.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:18.320
In Episode 1 of House of the Dragon, Alicent&nbsp;
Hightower studies the history of Princess Nymeria&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:23.040
with her companion, Princess Rhaenyra Targaryen.&nbsp;
Nymeria is considered such an incredible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:27.840
character, Arya Stark named her direwolf after&nbsp;
her in the original Game of Thrones series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.400
and HBO is already developing a&nbsp;
series about her, called 10,000 Ships.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:36.240
"She took Lord Mors Martell of Dorne to husband,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:40.080
and burnt her own fleet of Sunspear to show&nbsp;
her own people they were finished running."

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:46.000
The legend of Princess Nymeria begins about a&nbsp;
thousand years prior to the events in Game of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.640
Thrones. Prince Garin thought their people — known&nbsp;
as the Rhoynar — could hold their own against the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:56.400
dragon-riding Valyrians. Nymeria suspected he was&nbsp;
wrong, and when most of the men died fighting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:02.560
or were taken into slavery, she fled Essos with&nbsp;
mostly women and children on the 10,000 ships they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:08.400
had left. After a few extended stopovers,&nbsp;
Nymeria and the Rhoynar settled in Dorne,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:12.560
where she burned her enormous but barely&nbsp;
seaworthy fleet to make the point that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:16.800
they'd found their new home. At the time, the&nbsp;
Dornish were having their own game of thrones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:22.160
and Nymeria married her preferred candidate&nbsp;
for the crown, Mors Martell. She became the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:28.400
Warrior Queen, uniting the kingdom and ushering in&nbsp;
Dorne's culture of independence and gender parity.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:33.280
It can be argued that a series about Nymeria would&nbsp;
let audiences see one of George R. R. Martin's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:37.920
greatest heroines in a more nuanced light.&nbsp;
Since she lived so long ago, and what we know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:43.200
of her borders on myth, 10,000 Ships could&nbsp;
be an ideal vehicle for even more spectacle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:49.600
action, and romance than Thrones fans are used to.&nbsp;
For example, besides that unimaginably huge fleet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:53.840
the Rhoynar were defeated with an&nbsp;
airborne assault of 300 dragons.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:59.440
Some storytelling formulas are tried and true,&nbsp;
such as the trope of the reluctant adult forced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:04.480
to care for the precocious kid. Currently, you&nbsp;
can argue that the biggest guardian-child duo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:09.360
is the Mandalorian and Grogu, while Game of&nbsp;
Thrones has its own decidedly darker version&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:13.920
with Arya and the Hound. But George R.R.&nbsp;
Martin's novellas — collected as A Knight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:18.080
of the Seven Kingdoms — happen to contain&nbsp;
an even better one. And it just so happens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:23.760
that a series based on The Tales of Dunk and&nbsp;
Egg is reportedly a high priority for HBO.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.800
Dunk is Ser Duncan the Tall, a poor squire&nbsp;
from Flea Bottom who pulls himself up by his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:34.480
own bootstraps and white lies to become a great&nbsp;
knight. Egg is an upper-class boy in disguise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:39.520
who becomes his squire and traveling companion.&nbsp;
Their adventures are episodic and generally more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:44.400
light-hearted than the other yarns Martin spins,&nbsp;
but there's still an adequate amount of chivalry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:50.240
backstabbing, warmongering, seafaring, and sexual&nbsp;
tension to please the average Thrones viewer.

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:53.840
A Dunk and Egg series would also give&nbsp;
audiences the chance to see characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:57.920
in their youth that they've already met. A&nbsp;
Knight of the Seven Kingdoms begins roughly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:02.560
90 years prior to Game of Thrones and&nbsp;
frequently ties back into existing lore.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:07.360
For instance, beloved character Ser Brienne&nbsp;
of Tarth is related to Ser Duncan the Tall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:11.520
though Martin has not yet revealed&nbsp;
exactly how. But the Season 8 episode&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:16.089
in which she's knighted is not-so-subtly&nbsp;
titled, "A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms."

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:21.600
The most consequential event in George R.R.&nbsp;
Martin's entire body of work could be Aegon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:27.440
Targaryen's conquest of Westeros. Aegon is such&nbsp;
a pivotal character, the Game of Thrones timeline&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:33.840
revolves around him. Dates are recorded as BC, for&nbsp;
"before conquest" and AC, for "after conquest."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:38.320
As entertaining as it is to watch his family&nbsp;
line fight each other for the crown 100 years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:42.480
later in House of the Dragon, or fight&nbsp;
for their very survival centuries later&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:46.960
in Game of Thrones, we'd really like to see&nbsp;
the military campaign that started it all.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:52.240
Aegon Targaryen the First is probably the most&nbsp;
cinematic personality Martin has yet invented.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:58.080
This striking, hulking, blonde-haired, purple-eyed&nbsp;
man began his endeavor to unite the Seven Kingdoms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:02.240
when — as we find out in House of the Dragon —&nbsp;
he had a vision about a threat from the north.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:09.033
"Aegon foresaw the end of the world of&nbsp;
men. Tis to begin with a terrible winter."

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:14.320
Together with his sister wives, Visenya&nbsp;
and Rhaenys — yes, he married both of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:20.320
sisters — and their dragons, Balerion, Meraxes,&nbsp;
and Vhagar, Aegon managed to incorporate six of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:26.160
Westeros' seven kingdoms into his domain.&nbsp;
Some willingly bent the knee, while others&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:30.480
had to be convinced. Though, ultimately,&nbsp;
he was never able to subdue the Dornish.

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:35.360
Though he looms large in the Game of Thrones&nbsp;
universe, Aegon was a complicated person.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:39.520
There's enough material just in his tenuous&nbsp;
relationship with the Faith of the Seven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:42.880
to make for a compelling TV&nbsp;
series — let alone his wives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:47.680
his two very different sons, the six Kingdoms&nbsp;
he ruled over, and the many battles which won&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:52.370
him control. Alas, there's no Aegon the&nbsp;
Conqueror show currently in the works.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:57.040
Arya Stark — played by the perfectly cast Maisie&nbsp;
Williams — was one of the breakout characters of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.040 --> 00:05:02.080
Game of Thrones and one of the easiest to root&nbsp;
for. When we leave her at the end of Season 8,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:05.614
she informs her siblings that&nbsp;
she's not going back to Winterfell,

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:11.957
"What's west of Westeros? I don't know."

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:16.000
In Martin's novels, what's west&nbsp;
of Westeros is the Sunset Sea,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:20.560
a body of water that is believed to be too&nbsp;
vast to cross. So little has been written&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:24.400
about what lies beyond the shores of the&nbsp;
westerlands that the showrunners — or even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:29.680
Martin himself — could have a blast dreaming up a&nbsp;
new world for Arya and her shipmates to discover.

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:34.960
Exactly what that world would look like — like&nbsp;
Arya's voyage itself — could go in several&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:40.080
different directions. Some characters hold that&nbsp;
there are dangerous creatures, such as krakens or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:45.600
sea dragons, in the Sunset Sea. If HBO wanted to&nbsp;
lean into magical realism the way it has done with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:51.680
dragons, White Walkers, the Lord of Light, and the&nbsp;
Faceless Men in Game of Thrones, an Arya-goes-west&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:56.720
series would certainly allow creatives to get&nbsp;
fantastical. An explorer narrative could also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.720 --> 00:06:01.920
riff on themes related to Europe's colonization&nbsp;
of North and South America, but the main reason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:07.280
to make an Arya show is simple: more Arya! From&nbsp;
her time as Tywin Lannister's cupbearer to her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:12.080
world-saving dagger-wielding lunge at the Night&nbsp;
King, Arya was consistently at the center of some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:17.980
of the series' most iconic scenes. Unfortunately,&nbsp;
as of now, there's no Arya on the horizon.

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:22.960
In House of the Dragon, Corlys Velaryon has&nbsp;
several important posts. He's the husband of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:27.760
Rhaenys Targaryen, the one-time heir who was&nbsp;
passed over for Viserys' branch of the family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:32.880
tree. He's the Master of Ships, charged with&nbsp;
outfitting and commanding the royal fleet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:37.840
He's also master of the formidable Driftmark&nbsp;
Stronghold, acts as a moderating voice on King&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:42.480
Viserys' small council, and is the richest&nbsp;
man in the world. Corlys will get up to his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:47.120
fair share of plotting and battling in House&nbsp;
of the Dragon, but decades before that, he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:52.800
accumulated power and fortune as a young man with&nbsp;
unmatched talent on the high seas and in trade.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:57.120
Corlys' origin story will either be called&nbsp;
The Sea Snake — a nickname that comes from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:02.000
the name of a ship he designed and built — or Nine&nbsp;
Voyages, which were the number of journeys he took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:08.400
to far-off places like Pentos, Volantis, and the&nbsp;
Golden Empire of Yi Ti. Regardless of its title,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:12.800
it'll illustrate the far-reaching adventures&nbsp;
of this charismatic character before he was a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:18.560
fixture of King Viserys' court. In the novel Fire&nbsp;
&amp; Blood, Corlys is described as wise in peace,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:21.520
valiant in war, and someone who clings to life,

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:24.960
"like a drowning sailor clinging&nbsp;
to the wreckage of a sunken ship."

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:29.280
Though Steve Toussaint shines like sunlight&nbsp;
on water as Corlys in House of the Dragon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:32.480
a young actor would probably have&nbsp;
to portray him in the spinoff.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:36.640
While the proposed 10,000 Ships series&nbsp;
focuses on a one-way journey, The Sea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:41.534
Snake would have a completely different flavor&nbsp;
as an island-hopping, treasure-collecting romp.

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:46.800
One of the places younger Corlys visits&nbsp;
is Yi Ti, a thriving empire in the far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:51.840
east. The Sea Snake managed to bring back&nbsp;
silks and spices from the Golden Empire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:56.720
making him twice as rich as he'd been before.&nbsp;
Jorah Mormont also asks Daenerys to run away&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.720 --> 00:08:02.080
with him to Yi Ti after Khal Drogo's death in Game&nbsp;
of Thrones. But outside of these few connections,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:07.920
Yi Ti has a rich culture and a dramatic history&nbsp;
all its own — one worthy of its own TV show. HBO&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:13.120
is in pre-production on an animated series that'll&nbsp;
aim to tell the stories of the Golden Empire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:17.520
though no release date has been announced and&nbsp;
no other relevant information has been revealed.

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:21.520
While it'd be great to give Asian actors an&nbsp;
opportunity to play live-action roles within the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:26.880
Game of Thrones universe, the colorful and diverse&nbsp;
world of Yi Ti — which boasts lush farmland,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:31.040
basilisk-ridden jungles, and bustling&nbsp;
urban centers — can be beautifully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:35.040
rendered in animation. With a history&nbsp;
that stretches back thousands of years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:39.600
occasionally intersecting with Valyria and its&nbsp;
dragons, there's just as much drama between the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:44.400
various god-emperors who aspire to the Yi&nbsp;
Ti throne as any other royal family in Game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:49.200
of Thrones. A show that delves into Yi Ti&nbsp;
— a subject which George R. R. Martin has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:53.840
written comparatively little about — could&nbsp;
make for a refreshing change of scenery.

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:59.120
As Game of Thrones drew to a close, HBO began&nbsp;
mining Martin's novels for more content.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:03.200
The network reportedly met with potential&nbsp;
writers to develop pitches and assured them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:08.800
that no concepts were too weird. In total, about&nbsp;
15 spinoff ideas were considered. One of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:14.480
pitches that failed to get the greenlight was a&nbsp;
"superhero team-up" story about Westerosi gods.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:19.440
While that may sound a bit too much like Eternals&nbsp;
— Marvel's foray into ancient religions — a series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:23.920
that further explores the role of religion&nbsp;
in the Seven Kingdoms could be interesting.

00:09:24.167 --> 00:09:25.767
"Does House Tarly keep the Old Gods?"

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:30.489
"No, my Lord. I was named&nbsp;
in the light of the Seven."

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:34.880
Characters in Game of Thrones often&nbsp;
referred to their deities as "the old gods&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:39.840
and the new." The "new" refers to the&nbsp;
Seven — also known as the Seven Gods,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:45.920
and the Seven-Faced God — who became the deities&nbsp;
of the most widely practiced faith in Westeros.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:51.920
Followers pray to the Father, the Mother, the&nbsp;
Maiden, the Crone, the Warrior, the Smith, and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:57.680
Stranger — each representing a different aspect&nbsp;
of humanity. For example, a soldier might pray to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.680 --> 00:10:03.280
the Warrior for bravery before an upcoming battle.&nbsp;
This septad may or may not have been real people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:08.880
but their origins are from about 6000 years&nbsp;
before the High Sparrow wreaks havoc in Season 5.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:14.640
As in life, religious factions vie for political&nbsp;
power in Westeros with just as much fervor as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:18.960
any of the noble families. A show about&nbsp;
the Seven, that flashed back and forth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:23.840
between the Faith's founding and its influence&nbsp;
circa the original Game of Thrones timeline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:30.000
would likely be as dark, mysterious, and&nbsp;
morally ambiguous as the rest of Martin's world.

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:35.120
House of the Dragon is filling in the juicy&nbsp;
backstory of one of Westeros' most notorious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:40.880
families, and so far, audiences are happy to have&nbsp;
all the salacious details. It stands to reason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:45.520
they'd be just as curious to know more about the&nbsp;
other family at the center of Game of Thrones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:49.600
and HBO may have planned to revisit the&nbsp;
Kingdom of the North with a series called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:54.240
either Bloodmoon or The Long Night&nbsp;
starring British actress Naomi Watts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:57.600
It was to take place in the Age&nbsp;
of Heroes thousands of years ago.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.600 --> 00:11:03.440
They even spent $30 million on a pilot&nbsp;
before unceremoniously canning the project.

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:08.160
Though legions of Thrones fans would surely love&nbsp;
to see the unaired episode, from context clues,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:13.760
it sounds like it may have shifted its focus away&nbsp;
from familiar faces and places. Perhaps a series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:18.160
that sat squarely on the shoulders of King Brandon&nbsp;
Stark — the founder of Winterfell and House&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:22.800
Stark — would've fared better? Part of the fun of&nbsp;
a Bran the Builder story is that the man himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:28.160
may never have existed, though there are myriad&nbsp;
carvings depicting his great works, and his body&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:33.600
supposedly lies in Winterfell's crypt. According&nbsp;
to the companion book The World of Ice and Fire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:38.960
Bran's legend may be the result of a millennia&nbsp;
of exaggeration and conflation. Generations of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:43.520
Starks have been named after him, eventually&nbsp;
culminating with King Bran the Broken at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:48.240
end of Game of Thrones. We've seen the Seven&nbsp;
Kingdoms in chaos and decline, and now we've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:52.640
seen them at one of their high points in House of&nbsp;
the Dragon. It'd be fun to see them in the distant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:58.015
past as one of the franchise's most familiar&nbsp;
locales was in the process of being constructed.

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:02.960
When Game of Thrones ended in 2019, most fans&nbsp;
assumed that they were leaving behind the likes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:08.320
of Jon Snow and Sansa Stark for good. The&nbsp;
news of spinoffs was already in the air,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:13.120
and all of them were prequels. That seemed to&nbsp;
make sense, as George R. R. Martin has yet to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:17.520
complete his novel series, and Thrones stars&nbsp;
like Kit Harington were already moving on to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:23.120
other projects. So it took a moment for the idea&nbsp;
to register when HBO announced that it intended to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:28.880
make a true sequel about Jon Snow's life after the&nbsp;
deaths of the Night King and Daenerys Targaryen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:32.684
with Harington reprising the role&nbsp;
that made him a household name.

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:37.840
"I don't expect we'll ever see each other again."

00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:40.130
"I wouldn't be so sure."

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:45.040
Unlike the rest of the shows in development,&nbsp;
there's no source material upon which to base&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:49.680
a Jon Snow sequel series. All the potential&nbsp;
writers have to go on is that Jon exiled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:55.120
himself to the North after killing his aunt&nbsp;
and former flame to prevent further atrocities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:59.840
We can assume he's been living as a Wildling&nbsp;
again — maybe as their chosen leader — but even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:04.800
that is an open question. This much of a blank&nbsp;
slate could be a good thing or a bad thing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:08.000
but what's promising is that it could&nbsp;
be a chance for viewers to catch up with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:13.440
their favorite Thrones characters. One could&nbsp;
easily imagine Sansa, Arya, Samwell Tarly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.440 --> 00:13:17.600
and even Brienne popping up through cameos&nbsp;
now and then. Even more tantalizing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:22.283
it could elevate Kristofer Hivju's&nbsp;
character Tormund Giantsbane to co-star.

